00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.040
The first big pile of rocks.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.260
Yeah, the first big pile of rocks. But in a way, that's like a tutorial.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.540
It is. It's good game design in the first five minutes.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:14.440
Right, but of course, because it happens in the first like minute, I, you know, like that's my immediate impression.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:24.460
But then I was just kind of like taken back by like the graphic choice or even like the enemy choices in this game, I guess I would say is a better way to represent like how confused I am about it.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:36.380
I'm riding a dune buggy and these guys are just like, okay, if we all just stand across a field and shoot at you, we will be able to take out your car instead of you running us over.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:48.160
Well, the thing about these games that we've been playing more recently, these like side scrolling shooters, I feel like the only way that these things could happen in real life is if we've just taken them.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.360
We've gotten the drop on them.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.100
Like we're taking them by surprise.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:52.860
They were on some sort of walk.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.880
Like this was a an army wide like field day.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.380
It's really the only way like commando could have happened.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:03.320
You know, like when it's you versus an army, that's really the only way it goes down.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.060
It's like, okay, it's army field day.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:11.100
Right. I can understand like a ghost and goblin situation where it's like, you know, oh, your love interest has been kidnapped.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.460
So now you have to like, like it or not, go through this whole thing.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:21.560
But when you're like, yeah, when you're in the army, like it's no one ever like, who was the general who made that call?

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:27.200
Like, who are you to be like, okay, so our top secret fighter plane was stolen.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:36.180
So can you just drive a car through a and it is like through an island because you get this nice overworld map, which I actually thought was a nice touch.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.660
It's a nice map. Where it shows you like you're at, you're in stage one.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:46.060
It kind of reminded me of Trojan and ghosting goblins in a way where it's like, okay, here's where you are.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.240
Here's the final destination.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:53.300
So you kind of like are on one thing and then you have to go through like a series of bridges and then you get to the island.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.800
But it's like, this is a huge mission.

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:01.430
And we're in a world where clearly planes exist because one has been stolen.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:07.410
And apparently it was the army's only plane though, because you can only travel by car.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:14.150
So drive down, you know, 40 miles down to the Baja and go across that broken bridge.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.570
Like what happened to this, to this country beforehand?

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.110
Like why is the infrastructure so destroyed?

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.450
Right. Already? Yeah.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:21.570
There's landmines.

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:22.830
There's rocks.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:28.350
There's soldiers who again are not afraid of you driving 60 miles an hour at them.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.790
Why is this a stealth mission with one guy in an RV?

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:34.150
I'm sorry. One guy in an RV.

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:36.610
Yeah. That's actually like a preferred ROM hack.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:38.190
I would like to see someone add that.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:39.810
This is already an active battlefield.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:42.630
But anyway, the gameplay itself.

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:43.930
Let's talk about that instead.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:52.910
Yeah, yeah, yeah. So immediately for me, this one stands out a little than the other ones because it does take those racing elements as well.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:56.530
So it's not just like a side scrolling shooter.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:06:07.010
It's it also like involves like ramping up your speed to make a better jump because if you're just driving along at slow speeds, you can't make the full jump.

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:08.570
Yeah. And the jump is awesome.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:10.090
I'm just going to throw that out there.

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:13.230
It's pretty cool when it happens.

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:18.990
And I don't mind that they kind of made like some platforming challenges out of it.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.830
Yeah, I think that's a that's what sets it apart in these kind of games.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:29.810
The bridge level, for instance, does a great job of like being like, OK, you're this bridge is about to end.

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:34.250
So jump and make a decision about like which side of the bridge you're going to go on to.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:35.210
And I thought that was nice.

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:38.810
I actually enjoyed the bridge section the most in this entire game that I played.

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:41.090
Yeah, I think that I can agree with that.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:53.850
But but another thing that is that says this one apart, too, is that even though it is side scrolling and you can't force the speed along, you you do have to think about your speed as a as a car.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:07:04.330
Because if you're just trying to drive as fast as you can through the level, you're going to be bombarded by enemies appearing at the very like top of the side of the screen.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:13.230
Yeah. I mean, you can you have a modicum of control of your scroll speed just by virtue of like speeding up in your car, slowing down.

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:20.270
You can change your position in the field and how fast the field scrolls, but not stop it, obviously.

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:25.410
Right, right, right. Right. And they do play some tricks on you if you want to go too fast.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:36.710
Like one thing that I noticed about one of the features or I'm sorry, one of the mechanics of this game is every once in a while, either rocks will fall or missiles will get shot at you.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:38.370
The missiles are the scariest thing.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:44.550
Yeah, like you have zero reaction time pretty much to dodge any of these things if you're going at full speed.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:50.990
And I noticed that if you're going slow, the rocks will fall at a slower rate.

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:56.550
